From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msttsengine, sapi: The voice speaks (6508)

msttsengine's Speak and GetOutputFormat were stubs, and the "Wine
Default Voice" token named no engine: SpVoice and ISpeechVoice (VBScript's
SAPI.SpVoice) said nothing, and programs that read text aloud failed.
The engine now synthesizes with eSpeak NG (the system's libespeak-ng,
loaded when present): a sentence at a time, in the fragment's language,
at the site's and the fragment's rate, volume and pitch, writing the
audio in the output's own PCM format, with word boundary, sentence
boundary and bookmark events, stopping between sentences on an abort.
The voice token names the engine and is the category's default.
---
